Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 15
Author: Richard Henderson
Date: 1927-08-06
Byline: Submitted by Richard Henderson, Rochester, N. Y. Judge pays $10 for each puzzle printed.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-08-06_93/page/n32/mode/1up
Number: 15
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-08-13_93/page/n29/mode/1up


FROLIC#CORSET
O#FORE#ENOS#U
RS#SILENCE#OR
GAS#SLATE#ILE
EGIS#ORE#KNEE
TENNIS#RAISON
##COS###ANT##
SPERMS#BAKERS
HART#ADA#SPAT
INE#PLANK#SIR
RE#TAMMANY#DE
T#VETO#NOES#E
SEAMAN#ATTEST


A1. Name something that is a gambol. ~ FROLIC
A6. Name a strong supporter for women (obsolete). ~ CORSET
A11. What is the call of the golf bug? ~ FORE
A12. Who was a son of Seth? (Biblical). ~ ENOS
A13. Who wrote Treasure Island (first and last init.). ~ RS
A15. What is broken if named? ~ SILENCE
A17. What is the little companion of "either"? ~ OR
A18. What is a good thing to take on an auto ride? ~ GAS
A20. What did our parents figure on? ~ SLATE
A21. Name a suffix. ~ ILE
A22. Give another name for a shield. ~ EGIS
A24. Name something people dig for. ~ ORE
A25. What kind of joint is often exposed these days? ~ KNEE
A26. What kind of racket is often taken to court? ~ TENNIS
A28. What little fruit has a kick in it? ~ RAISON
A30. Name an abbreviation signifying union (plu.). ~ COS
A31. Name a busy little insect. ~ ANT
A32. What makes a whale of a good candle? (plu.). ~ SPERMS
A35. What people have a lot of dough? ~ BAKERS
A38. Who is very fond of his deer? ~ HART
A39. What is the heroine's name in Dickens' "Bleak House"? ~ ADA
A41. What do many families have for breakfast? ~ SPAT
A42. Name a chemical suffix. ~ INE
A43. What piece of lumber makes a good steak? ~ PLANK
A45. Name a title of respect. ~ SIR
A46. Name a prefix signifying "again." ~ RE
A47. What club is symbolized by a tiger? ~ TAMMANY
A49. Name a French preposition meaning "of." ~ DE
A50. Name a Presidential negative. ~ VETO
A51. Name Congressional negatives. ~ NOES
A53. What people like to make port? ~ SEAMAN
A54. To affirm. ~ ATTEST

D1. What do some people do when they owe money? ~ FORGET
D2. Name a preposition. ~ OF
D3. Name a Spanish article. ~ LOS
D4. What doesn't hurt when you have it in your eye? ~ IRIS
D5. Name something often being strung (plu.). ~ CELLOS
D6. What part of the earth is at the axis midway between the North and South Poles? ~ CENTER
D7. What word precludes repetition? ~ ONCE
D8. Where do little fish come from? ~ ROE
D9. Name a means of transportation (init.). ~ SS
D10. In what place is any little potato apt to find itself in the soup? ~ TUREEN
D14. What suggests wisdom but is always green? ~ SAGE
D16. What is a good listener? ~ EAR
D17. What is it some people use for butter or for worse? ~ OLEO
D19. What kind of person is genuine? ~ SINCERE
D21. What do poor dancing partners dance on? ~ INSTEPS
D23. Give a word synonymous with swig; nip. ~ SNORT
D25. What do darkies wear over their heads? ~ KINKS
D27. What is a doctrine called? ~ ISM
D29. Name a national vehicular organization (init.). ~ AAA
D32. What article of apparel is, figuratively speaking, What is seen in any window? ~ SHIRTS
D33. What is seen in any window? ~ PANE
D34. What sea-fish ascends rivers to spawn? ~ SALMON
D35. What fruit supplies the oil that lubricates the machinery of government? ~ BANANA
D36. What do prohibition agents do when they want a drink? ~ RAID
D37. What is the New York boy's playground? ~ STREET
D40. What prevents the flow of liquid? ~ DAM
D43. What is the most brilliant feature of many old men? ~ PATA
D44. What sort of "tie" does marriage often end in? ~ KNOT
D47. What are the conditions of heat and cold called? (abbr.). ~ TEM
D48. What adverb means in addition, still, besides? ~ YET
D50. Of what state is Richmond the capital? (abbr.). ~ VA
D52. In what direction from Kansas City is Nashville? (init.). ~ SE


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A53: What people like to make port? → SEAMEN

